# architecture.mdc — Interview Architect

```yaml
architecture:
  summary: >-
    Interview Architect is a free-first backend and system-design interview-practice application. A React single-page app serves a static, versioned curriculum and communicates on the same origin with a Hono API deployed as a Cloudflare Worker. The API stores anonymous learner progress in Cloudflare D1 while curriculum content remains in Git and free-form drafts remain local to the learner's browser by default.

  style: modular-monolith

  layers:
    - name: presentation
      paths:
        - apps/web/src/App.tsx
        - apps/web/src/pages
        - apps/web/src/components
        - apps/web/src/hooks
        - apps/web/src/styles
    - name: http
      paths:
        - apps/api/src/app.ts
        - apps/api/src/worker.ts
        - apps/api/src/lib/http.ts
        - apps/web/src/lib/api.ts
    - name: business
      paths:
        - packages/domain/src
        - packages/content/src
        - apps/web/src/data
    - name: infrastructure
      paths:
        - apps/api/src/repository
        - apps/api/src/lib/security.ts
        - apps/api/src/lib/rate-limit.ts
        - infra/migrations
        - infra/wrangler.jsonc

  boundaries:
    - The React application accesses persisted learner state only through apps/web/src/lib/api.ts and the useLearner state boundary.
    - Static curriculum and selectors live in packages/content; personal state belongs to the API and D1.
    - packages/domain stays framework-free and must not import React, Hono, Cloudflare bindings, or D1.
    - apps/api/src/repository/repository.ts defines persistence behavior; D1Repository is production storage and MemoryRepository is a test double.
    - Worker API mutations require anonymous-session authentication and a trusted same-origin request.
    - Written drafts remain browser-local by default; additions that synchronize artifacts must define consent, retention, and deletion behavior.

  integrations:
    - Cloudflare Workers static assets and same-origin Hono API
    - Cloudflare D1 SQLite database via DB binding
    - Anonymous HttpOnly session cookie named ia_session
    - Browser localStorage for learner snapshots and draft text in the current release
    - GitHub Actions quality workflow

  auth:
    userFacingPattern: Anonymous opaque session token in HttpOnly Secure SameSite=Lax cookie; only SHA-256 token digest is stored in D1.
    partnerPattern: No partner authentication or external API integration in the current release.
    configPaths:
      - apps/api/src/lib/security.ts
      - apps/api/src/app.ts
      - infra/wrangler.jsonc

  errorHandling:
    businessException: Hono JSON error responses with Zod validation failures, explicit HTTP status codes, and sanitized app.onError handling.
    codes:
      - validation_error
      - unauthenticated
      - forbidden_origin
      - attempt_not_found
      - attempt_already_finished
      - rate_limited

  diagrams:
    existing:
      - docs/architecture.md
    preferredFormat: mermaid

  repositoryRelationships:
    - primary: kritikamodi-17/interview-architect
      consumes:
        - Cloudflare Workers
        - Cloudflare D1
        - GitHub Actions
```
